   "text": "This SMILES was read region by region from the drawing and has not been checked with a cheminformatics tool.\n\n**Fragments identified**\n- **Maleimide end:** a maleimide linked through an N\u2013CH2CH2\u2013O\u2013CH2CH2\u2013O\u2013CH2\u2013C(=O) chain to a central tertiary amide nitrogen.\n- **Central nitrogen:** it carries two identical CH2CH2\u2013O\u2013CH2 arms, each ending on C4 of a 1,4-disubstituted 1,2,3-triazole.\n- **Each arm:** the triazole N1 bears a CH2CH2(OCH2CH2)2\u2013NH\u2013C(=O)\u2013CH2CH2 chain, which attaches to C2 of a benzofuran.\n- **Benzofuran:** C4 carries a \u03b2-D-glucuronic acid ether, and C7 carries a CH2\u2013O\u2013C(=O)\u2013N(CH3) carbamate.\n- **Drug payload:** the carbamate nitrogen is the N-methyl-valine of an MMAE-type peptide. The sequence is N-Me-Val, Val, N-Me-dolaisoleuine, dolaproine, then the norephedrine-type terminus (1-hydroxy-1-phenylpropan-2-yl amide).\n\n**Stereochemistry**\n- I took the stereocentres as in standard MMAE, with L-Val configurations, and rewrote the chirality tags for the direction in which I wrote the chain.\n- The glucuronide is written as the \u03b2-D form, with tags re-derived from the \u03b2-D-glucose SMILES for the order used here.\n- The maleimide, triazole and benzofuran carry no stereo.\n\nSMILES: O=C1C=CC(=O)N1CCOCCOCC(=O)N(CCOCc1cn(CCOCCOCCOCCNC(=O)CCc2cc3c(O[C@@H]4O[C@H](C(=O)O)[C@@H](O)[C@H](O)[C@H]4O)ccc(COC(=O)N(C)[C@@H](C(C)C)C(=O)N[C@@H](C(C)C)C(=O)N(C)[C@@H]([C@@H](C)CC)[C@H](OC)CC(=O)N5CCC[C@H]5[C@@H]([C@@H](C)C(=O)N[C@@H](C)[C@H](O)c6ccccc6)OC)c3o2)nn1)CCOCc1cn(CCOCCOCCOCCNC(=O)CCc2cc3c(O[C@@H]4O[C@H](C(=O)O)[C@@H](O)[C@H](O)[C@H]4O)ccc(COC(=O)N(C)[C@@H](C(C)C)C(=O)N[C@@H](C(C)C)C(=O)N(C)[C@@H]([C@@H](C)CC)[C@H](OC)CC(=O)N5CCC[C@H]5[C@@H]([C@@H](C)C(=O)N[C@@H](C)[C@H](O)c6ccccc6)OC)c3o2)nn1"
